From cd3121ff4b38d19177f4004eaaf1fdbebacd72a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:24:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 63/65] perf(chonk): window the joint sumcheck's round 1
 instead of materializing the round-1 tables

The joint MegaZK + translator sumcheck folded the full tables at u_0 into
half-size round-1 tables (about 86 MiB on the headline flow) while the full
tables stay alive for the PCS, which made round 1 the ChonkProve RSS peak.

Round 1 now folds the full tables at u_0 one 8192-row window at a time and
accumulates the edges of that window; once u_1 is drawn, the quarter-size
round-2 tables are folded straight from the full tables at (u_0, u_1).
SumcheckProverRound gains accumulate_univariate_over_range and
finalize_univariate (compute_univariate is now the full-range case of the
two), and the skip_entire_row scan is factored out so it can run on a window.

Output is unchanged:
- each window entry is computed by the same fold (fold_stride2) from the
  same operands as the round-1 table entry it replaces, and reads outside a
  window are the virtual zero exactly as reads past a table's extent were;
- the windows partition the round's edges [excluded head, effective end),
  the effective end is computed from the extents the round-1 tables would
  have had, the gate separator is indexed by absolute edge, and the offset
  area is read from window 0; field addition is exact, so the per-relation
  sums and the round univariate are the same field elements;
- each round-2 entry is fold_stride2_pair(fold of the first pair, fold of
  the second pair), the same two folds two fold_stride2 passes perform, with
  entries past the round-1 extent read as zero, so round-2 tables are
  bit-identical and rounds 2.. proceed as before;
- the transcript sees the same univariates in the same order and no
  challenge draw moves. Flavors with fewer than two real MegaZK rounds keep
  the materialized path.
